# Secrets — never committed. AGENTS.md security rule 13.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# Python
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.venv/
venv/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.pytest_cache/
*.egg-info/
dist/
build/

# Node / Next.js
node_modules/
.next/
out/
.pnpm-store/
*.tsbuildinfo
next-env.d.ts

# Local state
*.log
# ...except the harness's own run logs, which are evidence, not local state.
# scenario-offline.log is the only record that all seven cloud keys were
# proven empty inside the container, and the bench logs carry the per-rep
# lines and the pacing waits that no JSON field holds. Scanned: they report
# counts ("7/7 empty"), never values.
!harness/reports/*.log
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
Desktop.ini

# Generated API client (produced by `make gen-client`)
apps/console/lib/api/generated/

# BENCHMARK AND REPORT OUTPUT IS COMMITTED, DELIBERATELY (2026-10-20).
#
# It was ignored as "machine output". That was the wrong call for this
# repository: REPORT_DRAFT.md's whole argument is that every figure is
# traceable to a named file, and a clone contained none of those files. A
# reviewer could read the claim and not check it, which is the opposite of
# what the document is for.
#
# Scanned before the first commit of it: no key-shaped strings, no
# token/secret/password fields, no credentials in URLs, no settings or env
# snapshots. 772K across 69 files. Anything written here later must stay
# that way - AGENTS.md forbids committing secrets, and an artifact is not
# an exception because a harness produced it.
#
# harness/audit/ stays ignored for now: it is append-only, so every run
# rewrites the tail and every commit carries a diff of a log. Its integrity
# is checkable on the machine that holds it (`make postmortem` verifies the
# chain), which is a different kind of evidence from a measurement file.
harness/audit/

# The sandbox's working copy of the target's prompts. Regenerated from
# production on every seed, and the directory a model-authored patch is
# tried in - so an experimental prompt must never be sweepable into a
# commit by `git add -A`.
infra/sandbox-prompts/

# Baseline captures are measurements of a particular moment, not source.
harness/baselines/

# Generated OpenAPI document (produced by `make gen-client`)
apps/console/lib/api/openapi.json
